WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.740 --> 00:00:05.050
For fans of horror movies, Halloween isn't
just one day in October...it's an ax-wielding,

00:00:05.050 --> 00:00:07.340
monster mashing, year-round state of mind.

00:00:07.700 --> 00:00:11.080
But you don't have to be David S. Pumpkins
to enjoy the spookier things in life…

00:00:11.740 --> 00:00:12.860
"How's it hangin'?

00:00:13.540 --> 00:00:16.860
All you have to do is make sure you watch
the very best horror films that movie-making

00:00:16.860 --> 00:00:18.180
maniacs have to offer.

00:00:18.330 --> 00:00:22.660
Lucky for you, 2018 has already provided you
with plenty of horror movies you might've

00:00:22.660 --> 00:00:23.400
already missed.

00:00:23.890 --> 00:00:27.500
So hollow out that pumpkin and stick it on
your head: here are a bunch of horror movies

00:00:27.500 --> 00:00:30.740
from 2018 that you haven't seen...but probably
should.

00:00:31.520 --> 00:00:35.080
"We have such sights to show you…"

00:00:35.960 --> 00:00:36.800
Annihilation

00:00:37.080 --> 00:00:43.220
Beautiful, awesome, restrained, and challenging,
Annihilation is the best film of 2018 that

00:00:43.220 --> 00:00:44.820
odds are you haven't seen.

00:00:45.070 --> 00:00:49.500
The movie focuses on the aftermath of a meteor
strike that's given rise to an inexplicable

00:00:49.500 --> 00:00:53.580
phenomenon, with a wide area of Earth enveloped
in an ever-expanding shimmer.

00:00:53.760 --> 00:00:57.680
When four investigators enter to figure out
what's going on, they find a disorienting

00:00:57.680 --> 00:01:02.500
pocket world that's slowly remixing itself
in gorgeous, disturbing, dangerous ways.

00:01:03.120 --> 00:01:06.799
It's a horror premise that creeps up on you,
with the implication of the story being nothing

00:01:06.800 --> 00:01:08.380
less than the doom of the world.

00:01:08.829 --> 00:01:13.240
The second film from Ex Machina director Alex
Garland, it's a masterfully creepy movie that

00:01:13.240 --> 00:01:15.360
deserves more attention than it got in theaters.

00:01:16.120 --> 00:01:17.000
The Endless

00:01:17.360 --> 00:01:21.460
Indie filmmakers Justin Benson and Aaron Scott
Moorhead have spent their careers putting

00:01:21.460 --> 00:01:26.060
together a respectable catalog of genre-bending
films, and The Endless just might be their

00:01:26.060 --> 00:01:26.560
best.

00:01:26.720 --> 00:01:31.020
Casting themselves in the lead roles, the
writer-directors tell a story of two brothers

00:01:31.030 --> 00:01:35.909
who flee a suicidal UFO cult, returning in
adulthood to reevaluate the life they left

00:01:35.909 --> 00:01:36.400
behind.

00:01:36.580 --> 00:01:40.500
They discover that there may indeed be magic
at the heart of the hippie collective but

00:01:40.500 --> 00:01:44.960
if it's real, what does the otherworldly force
protecting the group want in return?

00:01:45.180 --> 00:01:49.420
Made for very little money, you only notice
The Endless' low budget because you're impressed

00:01:49.420 --> 00:01:50.440
by what they pull off.

00:01:50.810 --> 00:01:55.340
With beautiful cinematography and a gorgeous
California location, it's among the prettiest

00:01:55.350 --> 00:01:59.950
movies on this list, with a sensed-but-not-seen
horror at the heart of the story keeping things

00:01:59.950 --> 00:02:01.380
tense through the whole runtime.

00:02:01.770 --> 00:02:03.020
It's horror by way of H.P.

00:02:03.020 --> 00:02:05.160
Lovecraft, with a story that sticks with you.

00:02:05.493 --> 00:02:05.993
Lowlife

00:02:06.593 --> 00:02:10.393
It's not often that you get to call a movie
"unhinged" and really mean it, but Lowlife

00:02:10.393 --> 00:02:11.533
more than fits the bill.

00:02:11.773 --> 00:02:16.233
A violent, genre-bending almost-farce that
straddles the border between horror, high

00:02:16.233 --> 00:02:21.313
comedy, and human drama, Lowlife is admirable
for being both audaciously plotted and technically

00:02:21.313 --> 00:02:21.813
slick.

00:02:22.273 --> 00:02:23.753
"Not cool calling me a German.

00:02:24.273 --> 00:02:25.053
. You don't know my struggle"

00:02:25.453 --> 00:02:29.873
Set in the scummy underbelly of Los Angeles,
Lowlife focuses on a number of small-time

00:02:29.873 --> 00:02:33.753
criminals whose stories all converge around
an organ-harvesting plot gone wrong.

00:02:34.053 --> 00:02:38.493
It's a nightmare inspired by Pulp Fiction
but unlike most copycats, this one stands

00:02:38.493 --> 00:02:38.993
on its own.

00:02:39.493 --> 00:02:42.413
The end result is intense, hilarious, and
gross.

00:02:42.803 --> 00:02:46.273
Despite feeling like it shouldn't work at
all, Lowlife is one of the year's best and

00:02:46.273 --> 00:02:47.813
most savage thrill rides.

00:02:48.473 --> 00:02:49.113
Marrowbone

00:02:49.653 --> 00:02:54.843
A quiet, self-assured mood piece of a horror
movie set in 1969, Marrowbone introduces a

00:02:54.843 --> 00:02:58.153
mother and her four children in the northeastern
United States.

00:02:58.373 --> 00:03:02.213
After the mother passes away, the children
must maintain the illusion of a healthy family

00:03:02.223 --> 00:03:04.833
in order to avoid being made wards of the
state.

00:03:04.833 --> 00:03:08.813
At the same time, there's also a supernatural
threat within the walls, threatening to tear

00:03:08.813 --> 00:03:10.633
the family apart from the inside out.

00:03:10.923 --> 00:03:14.873
Marrowbone received middling reviews from
critics, having some controversial late-game

00:03:14.873 --> 00:03:15.993
turns in its plotting.

00:03:16.193 --> 00:03:19.793
But the twists in the story are elegantly
laid out; even if you don't like where the

00:03:19.803 --> 00:03:24.093
plot goes, it's still a well-designed movie,
accomplishing everything it sets out to do

00:03:24.093 --> 00:03:25.533
with patience and reserve.

00:03:26.113 --> 00:03:26.953
Downrange

00:03:27.233 --> 00:03:32.093
On a road trip down an isolated backroad on
a hot summer day, the tire of an SUV explodes.

00:03:32.533 --> 00:03:36.873
As the young passengers set about making repairs,
they're attacked by an unseen sniper, who

00:03:36.892 --> 00:03:40.313
shooter picks off a few victims, leaving the
rest to huddle behind cover as they try to

00:03:40.313 --> 00:03:41.653
figure out how to survive.

00:03:42.003 --> 00:03:46.373
Like all good horror movies, it's a situation
you can imagine yourself in, however outlandish

00:03:46.373 --> 00:03:47.133
it may seem.

00:03:47.383 --> 00:03:51.913
But Downrange is more than just a good concept
it's good filmmaking, with quality gore effects

00:03:51.933 --> 00:03:53.813
giving every bullet a real impact.

00:03:54.313 --> 00:03:57.973
It may devolve into campy territory by the
end, but it stays entertaining all the way

00:03:57.973 --> 00:04:01.832
through to watch the characters struggle to
puzzle their way out of danger if there even

00:04:01.833 --> 00:04:02.333
is any.

00:04:03.533 --> 00:04:05.193
Gonjiam: Haunted Asylum

00:04:05.513 --> 00:04:10.144
Based on the local folklore surrounding a
real-life creepy location, Gonjiam: Haunted

00:04:10.144 --> 00:04:14.693
Asylum is a Korean horror movie that wears
its found footage influences on its sleeve.

00:04:14.693 --> 00:04:18.753
Easily among the scariest movies on this list,
the concept of the movie is classic.

00:04:18.953 --> 00:04:23.233
Forget complex mythologies Gonjiam is about
spending the night in a haunted house.

00:04:23.473 --> 00:04:28.073
The movie follows a group of filmmakers on
a live horror webcast, trying to break a viewership

00:04:28.073 --> 00:04:30.993
record as they broadcast live from a notorious
hospital.

00:04:31.323 --> 00:04:35.813
At first, the program appears to be an exercise
in fakery, but the signs of a haunting become

00:04:35.823 --> 00:04:38.293
a lot more convincing over the course of the
night.

00:04:38.293 --> 00:04:42.022
Few horror movies capture a sense of paralyzing
dread like Gonjiam does.

00:04:42.022 --> 00:04:46.433
If you're looking for pure, terrifying, white-knuckle
horror, it doesn't get much better than this.

00:04:46.953 --> 00:04:47.753
Veronica

00:04:47.973 --> 00:04:52.172
You should never believe hype that says a
movie is the "scariest ever" in Veronica's

00:04:52.173 --> 00:04:54.493
case, it's not even the scariest movie on
this list.

00:04:54.593 --> 00:04:59.112
But this story of a young teen girl's possession
and slow corruption is a well-crafted descent

00:04:59.113 --> 00:05:03.453
into madness, anchored by one strong character
and her otherworldly struggle with evil.

00:05:03.713 --> 00:05:07.593
Veronica introduces the title character as
a caretaker for her younger siblings.

00:05:07.973 --> 00:05:12.573
Mature, capable, and kind, you can't help
but sympathize as something sinister begins

00:05:12.573 --> 00:05:13.573
to wake up around her.

00:05:14.033 --> 00:05:18.272
She resists the evil, defending her siblings
from harm like a true heroine which makes

00:05:18.273 --> 00:05:20.473
the movie's bleak ending such a gut punch.

00:05:20.733 --> 00:05:24.113
The overblown hype for Veronica naturally
led to a bit of a backlash.

00:05:24.253 --> 00:05:28.052
But take the movie on its own terms, and you'll
get a well-done, thought-provoking possession

00:05:28.053 --> 00:05:30.513
narrative not that scary, but it's good.

